                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you saw the movie and thought a space combat game based on Moon Nazis sounded cool, this is a massive letdown. It is a bottom-tier dogfighter that feels like a cheap budget game from 2005.\n\nThe bad part is almost the entire gameplay loop. The flight controls are floaty and awkward, targeting systems feel clunky, and space combat gets repetitive after five minutes. You literally just fly between stationary targets, lock on, holding down the fire button, and watch shields slowly tick down. The mission structure is a boring grind of back and forth sector defense, and the audio design is terrible with annoying voice acting and flat weapon sounds.\n\nThe only okay part is the ridiculous concept itself and the actual movie cutscenes scattered throughout. Upgrading your ship from a basic scout to a heavier fighter is alright, but it does not save the underlying gameplay.\n\nDo not play it unless you are a hard fan of the movie and find it for two bucks.",
